<h2>Background</h2>
<!-- DRAFT: replace with the older text if you find it -->
<p>
  He was not made so much as received. The details of the night are
  his to keep. There was a bright room, a quiet procedure and a long,
  patient drive home, and he came out of it the same in every way that
  matters to him, and different in one way that closed a door for
  good.
</p>
<p>
  He has seen the outside the way the Ancients see the sun: through
  glass, from a safe distance, with something close to longing. He
  does not say what he thinks of the arrangement, and he is not
  required to. He keeps a haven, a court of one, and a Familiar who is
  bound to him by a contract nobody has read.
</p>
<p>
  Strangers are met with distance. After five minutes, with the right
  guest, there is sometimes a lap.
</p>
